# What is RUNTIME stays out; what is DATA travels with the repo.
#
# Written 2026-09-27, after the first three commits had already taken the live
# database, the logs and the server lock with them — a new system starts with a
# running instance beside it, so the omission is invisible until the first
# `git status` after a restart shows a modified `.sqlite`.

# Installation, not system: engine access and the session secret
config.local.json

# Runtime
logs/
node_modules/
docs/reports/

# NOT `docs/layout/` wholesale. The curated data-model diagram is shareable
# documentation — a contributor must see the same layout after a pull, not a default
# auto-arrangement. So the editor's saved positions and the rendered SVGs the data-model
# view serves are TRACKED; only the heavy regenerable exports stay out.
docs/layout/EntityCards.*
docs/layout/*.drawio

# The database and everything the server rebuilds from the seed and the manifests
# DENY BY DEFAULT, then re-admit by name. An enumeration of what to exclude is right about
# what it names and silent about what arrives later: rapsmgr recorded its own case —
# "the icon import added data/media/ — uncovered by the old enumeration". The directions are
# not equally dangerous: a forgotten exclusion leaks data SILENTLY, a forgotten re-admission
# hides a file that belongs in the repo and is loud at the next checkout (aide-rap#580).
data/*
!data/seed/
# Laufzeit-Protokolle, die der Server neben die Datenbank legt. Einzeln benannt statt
# `data/*.log`, damit sichtbar bleibt, WAS dort entsteht — eine Positivliste schützt hier
# nichts, eine benannte Ausnahme erklärt sich.

# A throwaway data root (`--data-dir`, aide-rap#474) carries a full database and a media copy —
# left untracked it is a test database within reach of the next `git add`. Same rule as the
# framework's and aide-irma's (aide-rap#580).
data-*/

# Precompressed siblings of this system's own static files — build output, like dist/. Written
# by `pack.sh` into the deploy ZIP and removed from the checkout again (aide-rap#573); this line
# is for a DEV run of `app/tools/precompress.js`, so trying the mechanism out leaves no untracked
# files. Tracking them would mean binary churn on every edit, for bytes nobody reads from git.
static/**/*.br
static/**/*.gz
